Header
  + name := Big_show
  
/*cd lisaac ; lisaac big_show && ./big_show

  
  
Welcome to Lisaac Ω
A programming language designed to become the reference for teaching programming.
Lisaac Ω aims to provide a clear, consistent, and modern environment to help
students grasp the core principles of programming with ease and efficiency.

Developed at the University of Lorraine and the University of Strasbourg,
Lisaac Ω is the result of research and innovation in object-oriented and 
prototype-based programming models.



Created and maintained by Benoît Sonntag and Dominique Colnet.*/
Insert
  
  - code_show:Code_show := Code_show 
  
Public
  
  - main <-
  (
    show (
      "example/startrek/startrek.li",
      "game_show.li", "elit-view",
      "example/hello_world.li", "elit-view",
      "example/welcome/welcome.li", "elit-view",
      "example/misc/glyph_example.li", "elit-view", "no-run", 
      "example/CodEx/Tortue/dessin_maison.li", "elit-view",
      "example/CodEx/Tortue/tortue_show.li", "elit-view",
      "example/basics/factorial_example.li", "elit-view", "run", "1000",
      "example/CodEx/Fibonacci/fibonacci.li", "elit-view", "run", "v2 500",
      "lib/collection/collection.li", "elit-view", "no-run",
      "lib/boolean/boolean.li", "elit-view", "no-run"
    )
  )
